  "sourceTitle": "Patty's Irish Cream",
  "sourceText": "Patty's Irish Cream\nBy: Maria Boyer\nPublished: Wednesday, March 17, 2010 - 4:28pm\n\nIngredients\n\n\n\n\n1 cup Irish whiskey (preferably Jameson's)\n2 large eggs\n1 can sweetened condensed milk\n1 cup light cream\n1 teaspoon vanilla extract\n1/2 teaspoon almond extract\n1 1/2 teaspoons instant coffee\n1 tablespoon Hershey’s unsweetened cocoa\n\nPreparation\n\n1 Blend all ingredients in a blender. 2 Serve over ice or in a hot cup of coffee.\n\nAbout\n\n\nIf you are concerned about using raw eggs, 1/2 cup of egg substitute can be used instead. I have tried this in the past, and it works just fine.",
